# ApexMaps Rules

You are working with ApexMaps (`apexmaps`), the geographic data visualization
library in the ApexCharts ecosystem: choropleths (flat or as pixel/dot
lattices), bubbles, markers, hexbin density, arcs, and routes over a built-in
geometry registry, which can also be drawn as a hex tile map or over raster
street tiles.

- Docs: https://apexcharts.com/docs/apexmaps/
- npm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/apexmaps
- GitHub: https://github.com/apexcharts/apexmaps

## Framework wrapper detection

Check `package.json` before generating code:

- React: use `react-apexmaps` (`<ApexMaps options={...} series={...} onFeatureClick={...} />`)
- Vue 3: use `vue-apexmaps` (`<ApexMaps :options="..." :series="..." @feature-click="..." />`)
- Angular: use `ngx-apexmaps` (`<apx-map [options]="..." [series]="..." (featureClick)="..." />`)
- Otherwise: core API, `new ApexMaps(element, options)`

## Critical rules

1. `const map = new ApexMaps(el, options)` then `await map.render()`. render() is
   async (geometry packs load lazily). No CSS import is required (styles are
   injected when the first map mounts, into `<head>` or the map's shadow root;
   importing `apexmaps/apexmaps.css` is harmless).
2. Geometry comes from the registry: `geo: { map: 'world/countries' }`. Pack ids
   and aliases: `'world'`, `'us'` (states), `'us/counties'`, `'eu/nuts0'..'nuts3'`,
   `'jp/prefectures'`, `'fr/departments'`, and admin-1 for 15 countries. Only use
   a URL or inline GeoJSON/TopoJSON for geography the registry lacks.
3. Coordinates are ALWAYS `[lon, lat]`, longitude first (GeoJSON order).
4. `series` is a discriminated union; `type` is one of `choropleth` (default),
   `pixel`, `bubble`, `marker`, `hexbin`, `arc`, `line`.
5. Join data with `joinBy`: `'field'`, `['geoField', 'dataField']`, or
   `{ geo, data }`. Omitted = auto-detected. Recommended keys: `us` joins on
   postal abbreviations (`'CA'`), `us/counties` on 5-digit FIPS strings,
   `world/countries` on `iso_a3`, admin-1 packs on ISO 3166-2 (`'JP-13'`),
   NUTS packs on `nuts_id`.
6. Use `null`, never `undefined`, for missing values; values are numbers.
7. Licensed features (work without a key, with a watermark): pixel, arc, line
   and hexbin series, hex tile layouts (`geo.layout: 'hex'`, an `@hex` pack id,
   or your own `registerLayout` table), raster tiles (`geo.tiles` with a url),
   pattern/image fills, marker clustering, drilldown, linked selection,
   annotations, story context, self-registered projections. The `viewChange`
   event is free. `ApexMaps.setLicense('APEX-...')` removes the watermark.
8. Defaults are publishable: do not add projection/palette/legend/tooltip
   options unless asked. Packs bring their own defaults (`us` uses `albersUsa`).

## Series data formats

| Type | Datum |
|---|---|
| choropleth | `{ <joinKey>: 'FRA', value: 7.3 }` rows, joined by key |
| pixel | the choropleth's rows and join, drawn as dots; `shape` circle (default) / square / hexagon / diamond, `grid: 'geo'` (default, spacing in degrees) or `'screen'` (spacing in px, default 8), `size` `'80%'` of spacing or px; no `fill`; licensed |
| bubble | `{ lon, lat, value, name? }` (`lng` accepted), or joinBy to centroids; sqrt sizing by default |
| marker | `{ lon, lat, name?, category?, shape?, color?, size? }`; shapes: circle, square, diamond, triangle, star, cross, pin; `cluster: {...}` is an option, never a series type |
| arc | `{ from, to, value?, name? }`; from/to REQUIRED, each `[lon, lat]` or a geometry key; `geodesic: true` default; `flow: true` animates direction |
| line | `{ path: [[lon,lat], ...], name? }` (`coordinates` synonym) |
| hexbin | `{ lon, lat, value? }` points ONLY, no joinBy; `aggregate` (`count` default, sum/mean/min/max), `radius` in screen px (14), `minCount`, `gap` |

```js
const map = new ApexMaps(document.querySelector('#map'), {
  geo: { map: 'world/countries' },
  series: [{
    name: 'Unemployment rate',
    joinBy: ['iso_a3', 'code'],
    data: [{ code: 'FRA', value: 7.3 }, { code: 'DEU', value: 5.7 }],
  }],
})
await map.render()
```

## Top-level options

`chart`, `geo` (map, layout, projection, view, graticule, sphere, tiles), `series`, `legend`,
`tooltip`, `dataLabels`, `states`, `theme` (`{ mode: 'light'|'dark'|'auto', palette }`),
`interaction` (zoom/pan/rotate/selection/nearest), `a11y`, `locale` (the map's own
strings: zoomControls, breadcrumb, dataTable, noData, sizeLegend, drilldown),
`annotations` (licensed), `link` (licensed), `debug`, `responsive`.

```js
// Street tiles: ONLY on an unturned webMercator, which no pack defaults to.
geo: {
  map: 'us/states',
  projection: 'webMercator',
  tiles: { url: 'https://tiles.example.com/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', attribution: '...', minZoom: 4 },
}
```

## Lifecycle and API

- Update data: `map.updateSeries(next)` (tweens; do NOT destroy + recreate).
- Update anything else: `await map.updateOptions(partial)`.
- Events: `map.on('featureClick', ({ key, name, value, datum }) => {...})`;
  also `featureHover`, `markClick`, `drilldown`, `selectionChange`, `zoom`,
  `rendered`, `rotate`, `viewChange` (every pan/zoom frame:
  `{ bounds, center, zoom, k }`; `map.getView()` returns the same now), ...
- Camera: `map.camera.flyTo({ center: [lon, lat], zoom })`, `easeTo`, `jumpTo`,
  `fitBounds`; instance: `frameFeature(key)`, `resetView()`, `zoomIn/zoomOut`,
  `rotateTo`.
- Drilldown: configure on the choropleth series; navigate with `drillTo(key)` /
  `drillUp()`.
- Selection: `toggleSelection(key)`, `setSelection(keys)`, `clearSelection()`.
- Export: `exportPNG()`, `exportSVG()`, `getSvgString()`, `dataURI()`.
- Join debugging: `map.diagnoseJoin()` or `debug: { joinDiagnostics: true }`.
- Statics: `setLicense`, `registerMap`, `registerLayout`, `registerProjection`,
  `registerPalette`, `setGeoSource`, `listMaps()`, `catalogue()`, `mapMeta(id)`,
  `listProjections()`, `listPalettes()`.
- Teardown: `map.destroy()` (instance is not reusable).

## Pitfalls

- `[48.85, 2.35]` for Paris is WRONG (that is [lat, lon]); write `[2.35, 48.85]`.
- Do not host GeoJSON for standard maps; name a registry pack.
- Choropleth of raw counts mostly redraws population; use `normalizeBy: 'population'`
  or precompute rates.
- `{ value: undefined }` is wrong; use `{ value: null }` for no data.
- `type: 'cluster'` does not exist; clustering is `cluster: {...}` on a marker series.
- `curvature` on arcs is decorative and abandons the great-circle path.
- `selection.modifier: 'none'` requires `pan.enabled: false`.
- scale `type: 'threshold'` requires explicit `breaks`.
- Projections beyond the 20 built-in names need `ApexMaps.registerProjection()`
  first; palettes beyond the 17 built-ins need `ApexMaps.registerPalette()`.
- A hexbin has NO `joinBy`: it bins `{ lon, lat }` points. Rows keyed to regions
  are a choropleth (or a `pixel` series), never a hexbin over centroids.
- `geo.tiles` without `geo.projection: 'webMercator'` draws nothing (no error);
  no map defaults to Mercator (`us` uses `albersUsa`, most maps `equalEarth`).
- `--apexmaps-*` CSS variables work on any ancestor and apply in light AND dark
  mode; set dark values under `.apexmaps--dark`.
- `geo.layout: 'hex'` exists for seven region sets only (`us`, `au`, `ca`, `de`,
  `br`, `jp`, `eu/nuts0`); anywhere else it THROWS rather than falling back to
  real boundaries. Cells keep the boundary pack's join key, so the data does not
  change. Layouts draw with the `identity` projection, default zoom and pan off,
  and label by key (`CA`, not `California`).
